[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:72. A Car Called Bluebird]
[00:00.900]Passage 72 | 文章七十二
[00:02.680]A car called Bluebird. | 一辆名为“蓝鸟”的汽车。
[00:06.015]The great racing driver Sir Malcolm Campbell | 伟大的赛车手马尔科姆·坎贝尔爵士
[00:10.380]was the first man to drive at over 300 miles per hour. | 是第一个驾驶时速超过300英里的人。
[00:15.025]He set up a new world record in September 1935 | 他于1935年9月
[00:19.985]at Bonneville Salt Flats, Utah. | 在犹他州的邦纳维尔盐滩创造了新的世界纪录。
[00:23.075]Bluebird, the car he was driving, | 他驾驶的“蓝鸟”汽车，
[00:26.400]had been specially built for him. | 是为他特别制造的。
[00:29.115]It was over 30 feet in length | 它长30多英尺
[00:31.815]and had a 2,500 horsepower engine. | 配备一台2500马力的发动机。
[00:36.550]Although Campbell reached a speed of over 304 miles per hour, | 尽管坎贝尔达到了每小时304英里以上的速度，
[00:42.600]he had great difficulty in controlling the car | 他在控制汽车方面遇到了很大的困难，
[00:46.040]because a tyre burst during the first run. | 因为在第一次试跑时爆胎了。
[00:49.580]After his attempt, | 在他尝试之后，
[00:51.715]Campbell was disappointed to learn that his average speed | 坎贝尔很失望地得知，他的平均速度
[00:55.448]had been 299 miles per hour. | 是每小时299英里。
[00:59.660]However, | 然而，
[01:01.200]a few days later, he was told that a mistake had been made. | 几天后，他被告知出了差错。
[01:05.320]His average speed | 他的平均速度
[01:07.365]had been 301 miles per hour. | 是每小时301英里。
[01:11.415]Since that time, racing drivers have reached speeds of over 400 miles an hour. | 从那时起，赛车手们已经达到了每小时400英里以上的速度。
[01:18.235]Following his father's footsteps many years later, | 多年以后，马尔科姆的儿子唐纳德
[01:22.235]Sir Malcolm's son, Donald, | 追随他父亲的脚步，
[01:24.720]also set up a world record. | 也创造了一项世界纪录。
[01:27.425]Like his father, | 像他父亲一样，
[01:29.235]he was driving a car called Bluebird. | 他驾驶着一辆名为“蓝鸟”的汽车。